{"id":"DRKS00020382","src":"drks","title":"Treatment exit options for non-infectious uveitis","official":"","summary":"Uveitis comprises a group of rare diseases characterised by intraocular inflammation which may cause vision impairment and blindness, especially when the posterior segment is affected. When non-infectious, the disease is often treated with different anti-inflammatory drugs. To date, there is no registry for this rare disease in Germany or other industrialised countries. Hence, the treatment outcomes of common combinations of immune therapeutics are unknown. Thus, TOFU registry’s objective is to develop treatment exit strategies for patients with quiescent non-infectious uveitis on long-term treatment. Patients will also enter information on their quality of life via weblinks.","conditions":["Non-infectious uveitis of the posterior segment with or without immunomodulatory treatment"],"interventions":[{"type":"ARM","name":"Disease courses of patients with non-infectious uveitis of the posterior segment"}],"criteria":"Inclusion criteria:\n- Male or female subjects who are ≥18 years of age, on the day of signing informed consent\r\n- Ability to consent\r\n- Non-infectious intermediate, posterior or panuveitis or retinal vasculitis\nExclusion criteria:\n- Missing or unwilling to consent \r\n- Any prior therapy with DMARDs \r\n- Intravitreal therapy with dexamethasone, VEGF-Inhibitors, triamcinolone or sirolimus in the last 6 months\r\n- Intravitreal therapy with fluocinolone acetonide or methotrexate in the last 36 months\r\n- Intraocular surgery within the last 6 months\r\n- Severe opacities of cornea, lens or vitreous that preclude assessment of inflammatory activity of the posterior pole \r\n- Conceivable inability to attend regularly at participating centre","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"OBSERVATIONAL","purpose":"","enrollment":null,"start":"2019-08-12","pcd":"","upd":"2026-06-30","sponsor":"Universitätsklinikum Bonn","areas":["other"],"central":["Jennifer Dell · Universitäts-Augenklinik Bonn · 0228 287 15948 · jennifer.dell@ukbonn.de"],"sites":[{"f":"Augenklinik","city":"Aachen","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":50.7766,"lon":6.0834},{"f":"Augenklinik","city":"München","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":51.607,"lon":13.3124},{"f":"Augenklinik","city":"Tübingen","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":48.5227,"lon":9.0522},{"f":"Augenklinik","city":"Hamburg","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":53.5507,"lon":9.993},{"f":"Augenklinik","city":"Köln","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":50.9384,"lon":6.96},{"f":"Augenklinik","city":"Würzburg","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":49.7939,"lon":9.9512},{"f":"Augenklinik","city":"Chemnitz","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":50.8357,"lon":12.9292},{"f":"Augenklinik","city":"Düsseldorf","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":51.2232,"lon":6.7793},{"f":"Augenklinik","city":"Göttingen","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":51.5344,"lon":9.9323},{"f":"Augenklinik","city":"Heidelberg","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":49.4077,"lon":8.6908},{"f":"Augenzentrum am St. Franziskus Hospital","city":"Münster","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":51.9624,"lon":7.6257},{"f":"Augenklinik","city":"Münster","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":51.9624,"lon":7.6257},{"f":"Augenklinik","city":"Bonn","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":50.7344,"lon":7.0955},{"f":"Charité - Augenklinik","city":"Berlin","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":52.5244,"lon":13.4105},{"f":"Augenklinik","city":"Freiburg im Breisgau","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":47.9959,"lon":7.8522},{"f":"Augenklinik","city":"Sulzbach","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":49.2988,"lon":7.057},{"f":"Universitätsklinikum Augenklinik","city":"Homburg/Saar","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":null,"lon":null},{"f":"Dietrich-Bonhoeffer Klinikum Augenklinik","city":"Neubrandenburg","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":53.5573,"lon":13.261},{"f":"Universitätskli